Subject: [benchmark fixture] Stabilize updater input during row-tab click test

The row-switch test samples tab bounds and clicks them in separate renders.
Like the hint geometry test, its header width depends on global updater
state. Participate in the existing updater mutex across that interval.
Retain all original click, row-selection, and geometry assertions and
normal threading. This is independent of wall-clock animation settlement.

